-fields ["answer-field-5fe64433-8049-59a4-92e3-4b844a0413ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5fe64433-8049-59a4-92e3-4b844a0413ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "5fe64433-8049-59a4-92e3-4b844a0413ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1087e128-433e-5dbb-b41c-efc06f006327" :answer-field/choices ["answer-373345b9-6e58-570d-b2b5-72c292671f91" "answer-1087e128-433e-5dbb-b41c-efc06f006327" "answer-bae73f9d-b5cf-5078-ba21-b6b89757dd35" "answer-c2a2aff9-1ce4-524a-8327-6e76bd255f62" "answer-04be5953-70b3-58ac-84de-7aec8ff49e33"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-373345b9-6e58-570d-b2b5-72c292671f91" :answer/id #uuid "373345b9-6e58-570d-b2b5-72c292671f91" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12$ children" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1087e128-433e-5dbb-b41c-efc06f006327" :answer/id #uuid "1087e128-433e-5dbb-b41c-efc06f006327" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$14$ children" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bae73f9d-b5cf-5078-ba21-b6b89757dd35" :answer/id #uuid "bae73f9d-b5cf-5078-ba21-b6b89757dd35" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$16$ children" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2a2aff9-1ce4-524a-8327-6e76bd255f62" :answer/id #uuid "c2a2aff9-1ce4-524a-8327-6e76bd255f62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$18$ children" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04be5953-70b3-58ac-84de-7aec8ff49e33" :answer/id #uuid "04be5953-70b3-58ac-84de-7aec8ff49e33" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$20$ children" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5a809928-75f9-5540-949c-59cd2e66a5d3" :question/id #uuid "5a809928-75f9-5540-949c-59cd2e66a5d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-61163" :question/problem "A bunch of grapes contained $50$ grapes. Serena eats $28%$ of them. How many grapes did Serena eat?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the total number of grapes, which is $50$ grapes. The percentage is $28%,$ and the part is the number of grapes Serena ate.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n28%=28÷100=0.28\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =28%\\times 50 \\\\  & =0.28\\times 50 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $28%$ of $50$ is $14.$ Thus, Serena ate $14$ grapes.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n28%=\\frac{28}{100}=\\frac{28÷4}{100÷4}=\\frac{7}{25}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =28%\\times 50 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{25}\\times 50 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{50}{25} \\\\  & =7\\times 2 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $28%$ of $50$ is $14.$ Thus, Serena ate $14$ grapes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ceb325ac-a50b-51e2-bf5d-2c9c5d43b7fb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ceb325ac-a50b-51e2-bf5d-2c9c5d43b7fb" :answer-field/id #uuid "ceb325ac-a50b-51e2-bf5d-2c9c5d43b7fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-375b9c30-c252-598c-80f0-b9aa4d93803c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5bed1096-653c-5c18-8f32-375f32024b35" "answer-375b9c30-c252-598c-80f0-b9aa4d93803c" "answer-a0aa0a0a-e9bf-512c-8870-61088113d83b" "answer-44d8e748-b602-5fa9-95ca-8c3d9b2ac389" "answer-a581cf6e-89b6-5ab2-b324-834385f78789"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bed1096-653c-5c18-8f32-375f32024b35" :answer/id #uuid "5bed1096-653c-5c18-8f32-375f32024b35" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12$ grapes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-375b9c30-c252-598c-80f0-b9aa4d93803c" :answer/id #uuid "375b9c30-c252-598c-80f0-b9aa4d93803c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$14$ grapes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0aa0a0a-e9bf-512c-8870-61088113d83b" :answer/id #uuid "a0aa0a0a-e9bf-512c-8870-61088113d83b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$15$ grapes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44d8e748-b602-5fa9-95ca-8c3d9b2ac389" :answer/id #uuid "44d8e748-b602-5fa9-95ca-8c3d9b2ac389" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$16$ grapes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a581cf6e-89b6-5ab2-b324-834385f78789" :answer/id #uuid "a581cf6e-89b6-5ab2-b324-834385f78789" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$18$ grapes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147850 :question/problem "The original price of a toy robot in a department store was $$75.$ The store manager decides to reduce the price by $12%.$ How much of a discount has the manager given?" :question/worked-solution "To find the discount, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the old price, which is $$75.$ The percentage is $12%,$ and the part is the discount in dollars.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n12%=12÷100=0.12\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =12%\\times 75 \\\\  & =0.12\\times 75 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12%$ of $75$ is $9.$ So, the discount is $$9.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n12%=\\frac{12}{100}=\\frac{12÷4}{100÷4}=\\frac{3}{25}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =12%\\times 75 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}\\times 75 \\\\  & =3\\times \\frac{75}{25} \\\\  & =3\\times 3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12%$ of $75$ is $9.$ So, the discount is $$9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144854 :answer-field/correct 17592186144857 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-37153dd3-f5a5-5cb4-89d6-f95a95fd428d" :question/id #uuid "37153dd3-f5a5-5cb4-89d6-f95a95fd428d" :question/math-academy-id "q-61179" :question/problem "A party-planning company decorated a room with $200$ balloons. Of this amount, $7.5%$ of the balloons are white. How many white balloons are there?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the number of balloons in the room, which is $200.$ The percentage is $7.5%,$ and the part is the number of white balloons.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n7.5%=7.5÷100=0.075\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =7.5%\\times 200 \\\\  & =0.075\\times 200 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7.5%$ of $200$ is $15.$ Thus, there are $15$ white balloons.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n7.5%=\\frac{7.5}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =7.5%\\times 200 \\\\  & =\\frac{7.5}{100}\\times 200 \\\\  & =7.5\\times \\frac{200}{100} \\\\  & =7.5\\times 2 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7.5%$ of $200$ is $15.$ Thus, there are $15$ white balloons." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d042f82c-4cb1-56b8-b08d-5af028f1c43a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d042f82c-4cb1-56b8-b08d-5af028f1c43a" :answer-field/id #uuid "d042f82c-4cb1-56b8-b08d-5af028f1c43a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a756c6a-2